    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0262" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/>

                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">ministerial regulations determining the bureaus op
                        customs to be open to the importation of fresh meats.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The minister of agriculture and public works.</p>
                <p>See the royal decree of December 14, 1897, reorganizing the service of expert
                    inspection of fresh meats imported into the Kingdom.</p>
                <p>Upon the proposition of the minister of finance, decree:</p>
                <p>Single article. The importation of fresh meats after the 1st of January proximo
                    will be make exclusively through the bureaus and branch bureaus of customs which
                    are enumerated in the annexed table as a part of this decree, and upon the days
                    and at the hours indicated.</p>
                <p>The inspection shall be made under the direction of the experts whose names are
                    set opposite those of the bureaus and branch bureaus of customs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Brussels</placeName>, the <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1897-12-17">December 17,
                        1897</date>.</dateline>
                    <signed rendition="#right">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leon De Bruyn.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
